From 978b087e6300a36f03aab3c23858e9fe02d33d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:10:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 172/210] clk: meson: s4-peripherals: keep the video clocks
 running

The display driver programs the video clock tree directly, so the clock
framework sees the encoder and HDMI clocks as unused and gates them when
it disables unused clocks. On S4 the ENCI clock feeds the line reset
interrupt used as vsync, so vsync stops shortly after boot while the
HDMI output keeps running, and DRM times out waiting for vblanks until
the next full modeset re-enables the gates:

  [CRTC:46:meson_crtc] vblank wait timed out
  meson-drm ff000000.vpu: [drm] *ERROR* flip_done timed out

Mark the same video clocks CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED as G12A does.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

